* The memorial stone (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our own script and our
* own art from art/memorial.py). Run by openc2e after the world loads
* (Additions folder); safe to repeat.
*
* An Easter egg (owner, 2026-11-15): four norns that hatched within seconds
* of each other died of old age at the same moment, their genomes' lifespan
* run out together. A small headstone (2 3 254, sprite zmem) stands in the
* dark brick niche of the stone arcade west of the incubator (x 4996-5042,
* its plinth on the floor at y 1172), where few creatures pass (a sample of
* Home: 4 creature sightings in that part of the arcade in 3 minutes, against
* hundreds by the incubator). It is behind creatures (plane 900) and hidden
* from them (ATTR 16 + 4: only the hand presses it).
*
* Pressing it opens a window above it (2 1 159, sprite zmtb: a sandstone
* tablet) with announcement 40 (announcements.txt), and, once four or more
* that hatched together have died of old age together in this world, their
* names (41; the engine's lifeLogEntry::together, which also puts a
* "Together" notice on the status bar that leads here). A click on the
* window closes it; it closes by itself after 60 s. One window at a time.
enum 2 3 254 kill targ next
enum 2 1 159 kill targ next
inst
new: simp zmem 1 0 900 0
setv cls2 2 3 254
setv attr 20
mvto 4996 1118
slow

scrp 2 3 254 1
  inst
  enum 2 1 159 kill targ next
  setv var0 posx
  subv var0 170
  setv var1 post
  subv var1 244
  new: cbub zmtb 1 0 40
  setv cls2 2 1 159
  setv attr 4
  new: part 0 0 0 0 9100
  new: bbtx 0 30 44 280
  bbtx 0 0
  bbfd 0 66 54 42
  mvto var0 var1
  tick 600
endm

scrp 2 1 159 1
  kill ownr
endm

scrp 2 1 159 9
  kill ownr
endm
